{"base_rate":0.5135135135135135,"brier":0.26117695590327167,"bss":-0.04547149892274538,"bss_hi":0.06290144985147555,"bss_lo":-0.15106769055749544,"chart":{"base":[727.9,81.0],"fp":[456.1,273.1],"lead":"62,274.7 272,269.6 482,261.1 692,242.2","note":{"base":"skill -0.05 — higher than 9% of cities","fp":"low end +24pp, high end +22pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 85% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 27%; promised 95% → rained 71%"},"rel":"62.1,348.8 117.6,334.6 352.9,220.9 662.4,161.3"},"country":"NZ","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.21678520625889047,"ess":340.721379424515,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Auckland</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Auckland rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>78%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>27%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 703 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 17.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.05, ranked 193 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(179&ndash;199) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>27%</b></td><td class='num'>129</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>28%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'><b>33%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'><b>53%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'><b>61%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>84%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>78%</b></td><td class='num'>211</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Auckland</b> <span class=\"muted\">New Zealand</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-0.05</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>179&ndash;199\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>703 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Auckland &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Auckland\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.08232558139535,381.9294573643415 72.93707317073171,350.9268292682927 109.49090909090908,299.27272727272725 174.96351351351353,219.67567567567568 272.830447761194,115.7910447761194 355.1686486486487,47.51351351351349 409.4498578199052,18.0 409.4498578199052,24.900473933649266 355.1686486486487,106.54054054054052 272.830447761194,202.71641791044777 174.96351351351353,298.3783783783784 109.49090909090908,359.93939393939394 72.93707317073171,382.0 58.08232558139535,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"195.0810810810811\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"195.0810810810811\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.08232558139535,283.2403100775194 72.93707317073171,279.9024390243902 109.49090909090908,260.6666666666667 174.96351351351353,190.1621621621622 272.830447761194,159.2537313432836 355.1686486486487,200.0 409.4498578199052,99.08056872037912\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 27% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 129 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.08232558139535\" cy=\"283.2403100775194\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 28% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 82 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"72.93707317073171\" cy=\"279.9024390243902\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 15%&amp;#10;It rained 33% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"109.49090909090908\" cy=\"260.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 33%&amp;#10;It rained 53% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"174.96351351351353\" cy=\"190.1621621621622\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 61%&amp;#10;It rained 61% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"272.830447761194\" cy=\"159.2537313432836\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 84%&amp;#10;It rained 50% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"355.1686486486487\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 78% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 211 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.4498578199052\" cy=\"99.08056872037912\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(51%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Auckland the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.07) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.47).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>164</td><td class='num'>68%</td><td class='num'>-0.467</td><td class='num'>27.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>205</td><td class='num'>52%</td><td class='num'>-0.060</td><td class='num'>19.9%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>169</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>-0.017</td><td class='num'>18.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>165</td><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'>0.074</td><td class='num'>18.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":-36.84853,"lon":174.76349,"n":703,"n_cities":213,"name":"Auckland","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0002325581395348837,"n":129,"obs":0.2713178294573643,"sig":true},{"hi":0.09600000000000022,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.042195121951219515,"n":82,"obs":0.2804878048780488,"sig":true},{"hi":0.22,"lo":0.09600000000000022,"mean":0.14545454545454545,"n":66,"obs":0.3333333333333333,"sig":true},{"hi":0.46,"lo":0.22,"mean":0.3304054054054054,"n":74,"obs":0.527027027027027,"sig":true},{"hi":0.73,"lo":0.46,"mean":0.606865671641791,"n":67,"obs":0.6119402985074627,"sig":false},{"hi":0.9340000000000004,"lo":0.73,"mean":0.8394594594594595,"n":74,"obs":0.5,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9340000000000004,"mean":0.9927962085308057,"n":211,"obs":0.7772511848341233,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":17.2,"provisional":false,"rank":193,"rank_hi":199.0,"rank_lo":179.0,"reliability":0.05356837439423524,"resolution":0.04198449374653494,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"auckland","station":"","timezone":"Pacific/Auckland"}